      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Before settling on Belmont, the area was first called Pequosette after a local tribe, then briefly renamed Watertown.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.belmont-ma.gov/1704/Belmonts-History",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Two railroads once crossed Belmont—Fitchburg and Central Massachusetts—before both merged into the Boston & Maine system.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belmont%2C_Massachusetts",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1952, Central Mass tracks between Hill's Crossing and Clematis Brook were removed, rerouting traffic over the Fitchburg line.",
